post.description:
The chat API with accumulated response.

For requests from your local machine, authentication needs to be provided in the form of a temporary bearer token
found at "/auth/token" or by your base64 encoded Infineon user credentials.
A GET request with your basic auth credentials to "/auth/token" will return a permanent token without expiration.

(Slow)
To chat with images (gpt4o only) use the following history structure for public images:

```json
{
...
  "history": [
    {
      "user": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Describe the image"
        },
        {
          "type": "image_url",
          "image_url": {
            "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Infineon-Logo.svg/640px-Infineon-Logo.svg.png"
          }
        }
      ],
      "bot": ""
    }
  ]
...
}
```

(Faster)
For uploading your images use the following history structure and replace <base64_image> with your base64 image.

Example image to base64 in unix command:
`base64 -w 0 image.png`

Example image to base64 in python command:
`python3.9 -c "import base64; print(base64.b64encode(open('image.png', 'rb').read()).decode('utf-8'))"`

```json
{
...
  "history": [
    {
      "user": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Describe the image"
        },
        {
          "type": "image_url",
          "image_url": {
            "url": "data:image/png;base64,<base64_image>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "bot": ""
    }
  ]
...
}
```

